  "name": null,
  "problem": "Let ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{98}$ be a random sample of size $n=98$ from a population with a population mean $\\mu =180$ and population standard deviation $\\sigma =70.$ Find an approximation for the probability that the sample mean is greater than $182.$\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.0\\,$ | $\\,0.5279\\,$ | $\\,0.5319\\,$ | $\\,0.5359\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.5675\\,$ | $\\,0.5714\\,$ | $\\,0.5753\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.6064\\,$ | $\\,0.6103\\,$ | $\\,0.6141\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "",
